    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d927">

                <pb facs="1108" n="1098" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg1098"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Moscow/94: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-31T08:00:00+03:00">October 31, 1943—8
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1794. Personal for Secretary Morgenthau from the Secretary of State.</p>
                <p>Delam 45. In reply to my oral and written representations on the subject, I have
                    received a letter from Molotov<anchor n="72" xml:id="d927-f1"/> stating that the
                    People’s Commissariat of Finance will in the very near future send experts to
                    Washington to take part in the discussions concerning the International
                    Stabilization Fund.</p>
                <p>Please repeat to Secretary Morgenthau in the event that he is not in Washington.
                    [Hull.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d927-f1" n="72" xml:id="d927-f1-content">
